\par\par \b \uc2 Paramount Goes Back To 5 Days On Site\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jessica Toonkel \par \uc2 262 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 September 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Skydance\uc2  's Paramount is bringing employees back to the office five days a week, beginning in January. Staff members have less than two weeks to sign on to the new schedule or start talking severance.\par \par \uc2 Employees at the vice president level and below in New York and Los Angeles have until Sept. 15 to make their decision, Chief Executive \uc2 David Ellison\uc2  said in a memo to staff Thursday. Those not interested in shifting to five days from the current expectation of at least two days in the office can participate in an "opt-in severance program," he said.\par \par \uc2 The announcement comes just weeks after \uc2 Skydance\uc2  closed its merger with \uc2 Paramount Global\uc2  , the home of \uc2 CBS\uc2  , \uc2 MTV\uc2  and its namesake movie studio.\par \par \uc2 Company executives have said they plan to cut costs by more than $2 billion, and there would be reductions in head count later this year.\par \par \uc2 Paramount is the latest of many companies calling for increased in-office attendance years after the pandemic drove many to adopt remote or hybrid policies.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  said earlier this summer that white-collar employees who didn't want to abide by a new four-day in-office workweek, up from three days, could take a buyout.\par \par \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  and Amazon have also called employees back in large numbers.\par \par \uc2 "Being together in-person isn't just about showing up -- it's about actively engaging with the business, supporting one another and the team's efforts, and contributing to our shared momentum," he wrote in the memo.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250905el950000x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\