\par\par \b \uc2 McDonald\uc2 's Tip: Pay Workers More --- Burger giant says all workers should get base wage, including rivals' tipped servers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Heather Haddon \par \uc2 444 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 September 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 McDonald's\uc2  thinks sit-down restaurants need to give their servers a raise.\par \par \uc2 The burger giant has come out against wage rules that allow casual-dining restaurants, bars and other establishments to pay below the typical minimum wage to tip-earning workers.\par \par \uc2 McDonald's\uc2  has withdrawn from the \uc2 National Restaurant Association\uc2 , the industry's main U.S. trade group, as a result of its stance on the tipped wage and other issues.\par \par \uc2 "Right now, there's an uneven playing field," \uc2 McDonald\uc2 's Chief Executive \uc2 Chris Kempczinski\uc2  said on CNBC on Tuesday. He also said all classes of workers should be paid at or above the federal minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 McDonald's\uc2  critique adds a big industry voice to a yearslong battle, which has become more contentious as local lawmakers have debated whether to phase out the tipped minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 Chicago, where \uc2 McDonald\uc2 's is based, is phasing out the tipped wage. Washington, D.C., similarly decided to eliminate it, but this year paused its plans. Roughly half a dozen states, including California and Washington, have eliminated it, too.\par \par \uc2 The company has a vested interest in the debate. Sit-down chains such as Chili's have cut into sales at \uc2 McDonald\uc2 's by advertising burgers at prices that compete with fast-food meals. Paying tipped employees a subminimum wage is an advantage on labor costs that fast-food chains don't have.\par \par \uc2 The critique aligns \uc2 McDonald\uc2 's with labor groups and activists who have campaigned for years against so-called tipped wage rules. \uc2 McDonald\uc2 's declined additional comment.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Restaurant Association\uc2  said it "remains committed to representing the full spectrum of the restaurant industry and continues to advocate for policies that support sustainable growth and workforce development."\par \par \uc2 Tipping has become increasingly contentious as customers grow fatigued with digital prompts to round up bills at a widening range of businesses. Americans over the past year are tipping less, payment providers said.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has moved to eliminate federal taxes on tips for some classes of service workers. When asked about the no-tax-on-tips policy on Tuesday, Kempczinski said he supports the move but added that it won't help \uc2 McDonald\uc2 's workers, who don't receive tips. A fairer system, he said, would raise the tipped wage to the minimum set for other workers.\par \par \uc2 Most states still allow for the tipped wage. The wage, set at $2.13 an hour federally, allows patrons' tips to round out the rest of a servers' pay to reach at least $7.25 an hour.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250905el9500010\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
