\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 Unilever\uc2  to Shuffle Top Staff in 'Refreshing'\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kelly Cloonan \par \uc2 247 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 September 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Unilever\uc2  said it is evaluating its top 200 leaders and plans on "refreshing" about 25% amid a shake-up under its new chief executive.\par \par \uc2 CEO Fernando Fernandez, who took the helm in March, said Wednesday that the one-by-one assessments would aim to ensure that the company's leaders are the benchmark within the market.\par \par \uc2 "Are they good enough? Are they at the level that \uc2 Unilever\uc2  deserves?" he said at Barclays Global Consumer Staples Conference. "We expect 25% refreshing from that."\par \par \uc2 The company plans to fast-track emerging stars and bring in new hires, and has also boosted its incentive system, he said.\par \par \uc2 The planned shake-up comes after months of job cuts amid a wider restructuring plan as the company looks to improve its results.\par \par \uc2 Unilever\uc2  has reduced about 18% of its white-collar workforce in the past 18 months in an effort to bolster accountability within the organization, Fernandez said.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Unilever\uc2  has been an inconsistent performer," he said, adding that the company's results have struggled since \uc2 Kraft Heinz\uc2 's takeover bids in 2017. "Time flies and things change a lot, as you know, but that really derailed \uc2 Unilever\uc2  a lot. We lost our focus on volume growth."\par \par \uc2 The company continues to target 800 million euros, or $933.5 million, in savings by the end of 2026, and will deliver 650 million euros in savings by the end of this year, he said.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250904el9400022\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
