\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 Conoco\uc2  Cuts Quarter of Staff --- Driller follows move by rival \uc2 Chevron\uc2  to reduce workforce by as much as 20%\b0\par\par\uc2 By Benoit Morenne and Connor Hart \par \uc2 601 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 September 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ConocoPhillips\uc2  on Wednesday became the latest major oil company to announce layoffs.\par \par \uc2 The Houston-based crude producer said it would cut up to a quarter of its workforce, or about 3,250 employees.\par \par \uc2 The news follows \uc2 Chevron\uc2 's announcement earlier this year that it would shrink its workforce by up to 20%.\par \par \uc2 ConocoPhillips\uc2  said the layoffs would affect both employees and contractors, with most of the reductions set to occur this year. Its global workforce is about 13,000.\par \par \uc2 "We are always looking at how we can be more efficient with the resources we have," a \uc2 ConocoPhillips\uc2  spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 Shares fell 4.4% to $94.65 Wednesday, extending their 13% decline over the past year.\par \par \uc2 The layoffs come as President Trump has promised a golden age for fossil fuels. His administration has thrown its weight behind the oil-and-gas industry. It has opened up more U.S. land and water to drillers, greenlighted new terminals to export natural gas and accelerated new oil-and-gas projects, among other actions.\par \par \uc2 But Trump's trade policies have injected uncertainty into the global economy that has weighed on oil prices. This, combined with the fact that the \uc2 Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries\uc2  has been adding new barrels into already well-supplied global markets, has clouded drillers' prospects and prompted them to slow down activity.\par \par \uc2 U.S. oil prices are hovering around $64 a barrel -- below the break-even point for many of the industry's smaller players -- down from about $76 the week Trump took office.\par \par \uc2 In the Permian Basin, the largest oil basin in the U.S., drillers contending with lower oil prices and the impact of 50% tariffs on steel have shed rigs and crews that frack wells. \uc2 The Energy Information Administration\uc2  projects that U.S. crude-oil production will drop from about 13.4 million barrels a day in July to a little over 13 million at the end of next year.\par \par \uc2 "Price now is [a] disaster for the Permian Basin," said Curtis Leonard, a Texas oilman. "Inflation is killing us on insurance cost, pipe cost, supplies and labor."\par \par \uc2 The slowdown seems to have crept into labor data. Between the months of January and July, the number of U.S. employees working in oil and gas extraction fell by a little over 1%, according to preliminary data by the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The market-driven damper comes on top of an offshoring trend among oil behemoths such as \uc2 Chevron\uc2 , \uc2 BP\uc2  and others. The oil giants are moving more specialized white-collar positions and related work to lower-cost labor pools in countries such as India, while cutting thousands of jobs elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Chevron\uc2  cuts, announced in February, were expected to affect roughly up to 8,000 employees. The company said it was changing its organizational structure and would rely more on global centers around the world. Last summer, the company announced a $1 billion investment in India to develop an "engineering and innovation" hub in Bellandur, with plans to add 600 jobs there by this year's end.\par \par \uc2 Chevron\uc2  still wants to pump one million barrels a day out of the Permian Basin, where it drills most of its wells in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 On an earnings call with analysts last month, \uc2 ConocoPhillips\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Ryan Lance\uc2  said the company expected global oil demand to keep growing in the coming few years and expressed confidence that the outlook would brighten for crude producers.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250904el940001z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
89
