\par\par \b \uc2 With Vote Result Too Close to Call, \uc2 UAW\uc2  Claims EV-Battery Plant Win\b0\par\par\uc2 By Christopher Otts \par \uc2 749 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 August 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A high-stakes contest over \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  representation at \uc2 Ford Motor\uc2 's first U.S. electric-vehicle battery plant will come down to a handful of disputed ballots.\par \par \uc2 Rank-and-file workers at the BlueOval SK plant in Glendale, Ky., voted 526-515 in favor of the \uc2 UAW\uc2  this week, with 41 challenged ballots outstanding, according to the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 , the federal agency that oversees union elections. The \uc2 NLRB\uc2  said 1,249 voters were eligible.\par \par \uc2 The razor-close Kentucky election will determine whether the \uc2 UAW\uc2  secures a foothold at all three of the traditional Detroit automakers' new battery plants -- a vital step for the union to maintain its influence as it looks at expanding to other automakers.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  claimed victory, saying the disputed ballots shouldn't count. BlueOval SK, a joint venture of Ford and South Korea's SK On, said "each eligible vote" should count.\par \par \uc2 Some BlueOval SK workers who opposed the union said they are worried about their plant's survival after the electric-vehicle market hasn't materialized the way Ford and other automakers anticipated.\par \par \uc2 "I think if we go in there asking for $30 an hour for the production [workers] and close to $50 an hour for maintenance [workers] -- yeah, we could get that, but we could also close the doors and nobody'll have a job," said Rodney Page Jr., 44, a maintenance technician.\par \par \uc2 Bill Wilmoth, a production operator who supported the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , said he wasn't persuaded by the company's rhetoric about keeping his voice and "direct relationship" with management.\par \par \uc2 "Sometimes it feels like that's their way of saying, 'Just, just be quiet and do as you're told,'" Wilmoth said.\par \par \uc2 At issue with the disputed ballots is whether the workers who cast them were eligible to participate in the election: full-time hourly workers, such as production operators and maintenance technicians, at the plant as of mid-July.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , which will determine how to handle the ballots, didn't respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  President Shawn Fain's plan to expand the \uc2 UAW\uc2 's reach within the auto industry has stalled, and failing to secure union status at all the American automakers' new battery plants would be a setback.\par \par \uc2 After conducting strikes against key plants of the Detroit Three automakers in 2023, the union negotiated a streamlined path to represent workers at \uc2 General Motors\uc2 ' \uc2 Ultium Cells\uc2  plants in Tennessee and Ohio, and at \uc2 Jeep\uc2 - and Ram-parent \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 's battery plant, called StarPlus Energy, in Kokomo, Ind.\par \par \uc2 No such deal was made with Ford, however, and BlueOval SK has gone to great lengths to keep the \uc2 UAW\uc2  out of the Kentucky plant.\par \par \uc2 In a message ahead of the vote, BlueOval SK CEO Michael Adams implored his employees not to "turn your voice over to the \uc2 UAW\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The company spent about $82,500 on online ads -- mostly \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2  posts meant to convince workers that the union isn't right for them -- according to public disclosures by \uc2 Meta\uc2 , which owns the platforms.\par \par \uc2 "Our team members have endured months of union sales tactics and slanders against their exciting jobs and proud accomplishments," a BlueOval SK spokeswoman said ahead of the vote.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Fain's plan to capitalize on the big raises the \uc2 UAW\uc2  won from the Detroit automakers in 2023 has stalled. The union organized one new auto-assembly factory -- \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  in Chattanooga, Tenn. -- but after 16 months it has yet to reach a first labor contract there.\par \par \uc2 Workers at a \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  plant in Alabama last year rejected \uc2 UAW\uc2  representation, and the union hasn't made enough progress to force votes at other targets such as \uc2 Toyota\uc2 , Hyundai and Tesla.\par \par \uc2 Battery plants have emerged as an important front for the \uc2 UAW\uc2  to show it can deliver high wages, generous healthcare coverage and annual profit-sharing checks to members.\par \par \uc2 At GM's \uc2 Ultium Cells\uc2  battery plants in Ohio and Tennessee, production operators start with hourly pay of nearly $28, compared with $21 for workers at the BlueOval SK plant in Kentucky, who then get $23.50 after three months.\par \par \uc2 Ultium Cells\uc2 ' \uc2 UAW\uc2  employees are owed the same annual profit-sharing checks as GM's regular auto workers, which averaged $14,500 for those who worked full time in 2024. Ford's assembly plant workers got a little more than $10,000 on average for their work in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250829el8t0000r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
