\par\par \b \uc2 Whole Foods Staff to Join \uc2 Amazon\uc2  --- Move aims to fuse e-commerce giant's grocery teams and ease collaboration\b0\par\par\uc2 By Owen Tucker-Smith \par \uc2 646 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 August 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Amazonification of \uc2 Whole Foods Market\uc2  is nearly complete.\par \par \uc2 On Nov. 10, \uc2 Amazon.com\uc2  plans to extend new employment offers to \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2 ' U.S. corporate employees, according to an internal memo viewed by The Wall Street Journal. The employees, who work in roles including marketing and merchandising, will have about a month to review their new titles, salaries and benefits.\par \par \uc2 The move is designed to bring \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's grocery teams closer together and ease collaboration and innovation, said a spokeswoman, Lauren Snyder.\par \par \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  corporate employees will have access to an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  discount and healthcare benefits. They will lose certain \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  perks, such as their in-store discount and four weeks of remote work a year, the memo said.\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Amazon\uc2  spent $13.7 billion to buy \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  in 2017, the Austin, Texas-based grocer was primarily regarded as a high-end chain known for natural foods and specialty products.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  centralized \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2 ' operations and invested to expand the grocer's private-label brand and volume of conventional grocery offerings. It also used stores to serve as hubs for \uc2 Amazon\uc2  package pickups and online returns and incorporated a discount for \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Prime subscribers.\par \par \uc2 Those investments haven't always guaranteed more shoppers coming into grocery stores. \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  has lost market share of customers' grocery spending since 2019, according to the research firm Numerator. Bigger retailers such as \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and \uc2 Costco Wholesale\uc2  have posted increases.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  said that since the acquisition, \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  has expanded to more than 535 locations, while sales have risen more than 40%. In May, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Chief Executive Officer \uc2 Andy Jassy\uc2  told shareholders that \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  was growing "meaningfully faster" than the broader grocery industry.\par \par \uc2 During that time, the company has allowed \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  to retain its own job titles, its own benefits and, until recently, its own dedicated CEO.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  in January appointed \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  CEO \uc2 Jason Buechel\uc2  to run its worldwide grocery-store division. The unit includes \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  as well as the bricks-and-mortar and online chain Amazon Fresh, and \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Go, the company's banner of cashierless convenience stores.\par \par \uc2 Buechel, who has served as \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  CEO since the 2022 retirement of co-founder \uc2 John Mackey\uc2 , has been reorganizing the division to bring the chain closer to \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's other grocery businesses.\par \par \uc2 "Our current reality does not take advantage of the breadth of talent, resources, and knowledge" across the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  grocery landscape, he wrote in a June note viewed by the Journal.\par \par \uc2 Within \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2 ' corporate ranks, some employees have wondered what transitioning to \uc2 Amazon\uc2  will mean for their futures.\par \par \uc2 "These last several years, it's been a steady ratcheting back of the type of perks and culture and energy and enthusiasm that always made \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  a wonderful place to work," said Errol Schweizer, a former \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  vice president and author of the Checkout Grocery Update, an industry newsletter.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  said it has worked to preserve each of its brands' identities and that the reorganization is meant to propel collaboration and innovation.\par \par \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  systems are expected to shift to \uc2 Amazon\uc2  on Dec. 8, the internal memo said.\par \par \uc2 Starting next year, instead of an annual bonus, the grocer's corporate employees will receive \uc2 Amazon\uc2  stock as part of their compensation package.\par \par \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  corporate employees will retain their 20% discount at the chain for about a year, but come 2027 the perk will be reserved for in-store workers.\par \par \uc2 Starting in December, corporate staff will receive a 10% discount on \uc2 Amazon.com\uc2  for up to $100 a year, the company said.\par \par \uc2 This month, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  said it would expand its employee-discount program to include nearly all grocery purchases in stores and online in an effort to recruit and retain staff.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw262\pich446\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3930\pichgoal6690
