\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- Chili's Hands Out Fat Bonuses to Staff After Record-Setting Sales\b0\par\par\uc2 By Heather Haddon \par \uc2 497 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 August 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B9\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Chili's is serving up beefy bonuses to its corporate workers after a record year of sales and profit.\par \par \uc2 Parent company \uc2 Brinker International\uc2  on Friday was set to pay out bonuses at 200% of corporate workers' target rate, after the casual-dining company delivered its highest sales and profit for a fiscal year since Chili's went public in 1984. The company's net income for its fiscal year ended June 25 more than doubled the prior year's total, and sales increased 22%.\par \par \uc2 "This year's bonus is our biggest yet, and it's a direct result of everything you did to make FY25 one for the history books," the company said in a message viewed by The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 Chili's has become the poster child for success in the otherwise challenged restaurant industry, winning over price-sensitive diners by aggressively marketing its value and cultivating a lighthearted vibe on social media. The chain's turnaround, steered by Brinker Chief Executive \uc2 Kevin Hochman\uc2  since he joined in 2022, has helped the company more than double its share price over the past 12 months.\par \par \uc2 The Dallas-based company had 667 restaurant support center employees as of June, according to a filing. The company said it also gave record bonuses this year to its 4,500 Chili's restaurant managers.\par \par \uc2 Brinker\uc2  said it was proud of its performance and that the bonuses help attract and retain top-level talent.\par \par \uc2 Chili's has lured new customers with $10.99 burger specials that include bottomless chips and salsa and a drink, while advertising their meals as higher quality and with bigger portions than fast food. Younger customers have taken to their fried offerings, posting videos of themselves slowly pulling apart mozzarella cheese sticks on TikTok.\par \par \uc2 Applebee's and other rivals are now trying to replicate Chili's success, introducing burger deals for around $10 and raising their profiles on social media.\par \par \uc2 Fast-food chains are trying to regain their own mojo after cash-strapped consumers have balked at their prices. Restaurant industry traffic is down around 1.8% so far this year, and has fallen about 2.8% at fast-food eateries, according to market-research firm Black Box Intelligence. At casual-dining chains, however, traffic is around 1% higher.\par \par \uc2 While Chili's doles out raises, other chains are tightening their purse strings. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  on Monday said it would give 2% raises to its corporate workers, breaking from its previous practice that allowed for merit-based pay. The coffee chain said it needs to invest in overhauling its cafes while conserving cash elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Some investors are wondering how long Chili's can keep up its momentum, particularly as it faces tougher year-over-year comparisons going forward. Hochman told investors earlier this month that continuing to improve Chili's offerings, like its ribs and frozen margaritas, will help sales continue to grow.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw262\pich467\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3930\pichgoal7005
