\par\par \b \uc2 Meta\uc2  Freezes AI Hiring After Spree\b0\par\par\uc2 By Meghan Bobrowsky \par \uc2 536 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 August 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2  has frozen hiring in its artificial-intelligence division after spending months scooping up 50-plus AI researchers and engineers, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The hiring freeze, which went into effect last week and coincides with a broader restructuring of the group, also prohibits current employees from moving across teams inside the division. The duration of the freeze wasn't communicated internally.\par \par \uc2 There may be exceptions to the block on external hires, but they would need permission from \uc2 Meta\uc2 's chief AI officer, \uc2 Alexandr Wang\uc2 , the people said.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Meta\uc2  spokesperson confirmed the freeze, characterizing it as "basic organizational planning: creating a solid structure for our new superintelligence efforts after bringing people on board and undertaking yearly budgeting and planning exercises."\par \par \uc2 While all of the top AI companies have hired aggressively this year, it is \uc2 Meta\uc2  that has most often pushed the pace of the talent war, offering prized researchers pay packages worth nine figures and using "reverse acquihires" to strip startups of key leaders. Analysts have voiced concerns about the scale of leading tech firms' investments, with some singling out \uc2 Meta\uc2 's fast-rising stock-based compensation costs as a potential threat to shareholder returns.\par \par \uc2 The recent restructuring inside \uc2 Meta\uc2  divides its AI efforts into four teams: one working on superintelligence, called TBD Lab, that houses many of the new hires; a second working on AI products; a third working on infrastructure and a fourth dedicated to projects with a longer time horizon and more exploration, the people said. The latter, called Fundamental AI Research, remains largely untouched in the reorganization.\par \par \uc2 The four groups sit within the umbrella of Meta Superintelligence Labs, a name that reflects Chief Executive \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2 's recent emphasis on building computer systems that can outperform the smartest humans on cognitive tasks. The Information previously reported some details of \uc2 Meta\uc2 's AI reorganization.\par \par \uc2 Previously, \uc2 Meta\uc2  had another team called AGI Foundations, which worked on the latest versions of the company's large language models, known as Llama.\par \par \uc2 The team drew criticism from executives this spring after the release of the latest Llama models underperformed expectations. It was dissolved as part of the reorganization.\par \par \uc2 At least three members of the previous AGI Foundations team announced internally that they were leaving the company around the time of \uc2 Meta\uc2 's latest vesting date, Aug. 15, according to internal posts viewed by The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 It was after the Llama model release in April that Zuckerberg got personally involved in recruiting AI researchers. He approached employees of \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , \uc2 Google DeepMind\uc2  and other labs with email overtures and WhatsApp messages that quickly led to offers that in some cases reached $100 million in total compensation.\par \par \uc2 His offer to one researcher -- \uc2 Thinking Machines Lab\uc2  co-founder Andrew Tulloch -- could have been worth as much as $1.5 billion. (Tulloch declined.)\par \par \uc2 To spearhead \uc2 Meta\uc2 's AI efforts, Zuckerberg hired \uc2 Scale AI\uc2  co-founder Wang, securing him by paying $14 billion for a stake in his company. He also brought on former \uc2 GitHub\uc2  CEO \uc2 Nat Friedman\uc2  and \uc2 Safe Superintelligence\uc2  co-founder Daniel Gross, whose courtship involved \uc2 Meta\uc2  offering to buy a stake in their venture firm.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250821el8l0001p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
