\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 Meta\uc2 's TBD Lab Tackles New Version of LLM Llama --- Superintelligence AI group ramps up research and work with other teams\b0\par\par\uc2 By Meghan Bobrowsky \par \uc2 526 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 August 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 About one month in, \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2 ' much-hyped new team devoted to building machine superintelligence has a name, an initial project -- and a fast-growing list of employees poached from other artificial-intelligence labs.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this summer, the company placed all its AI efforts under a new umbrella group, Meta Superintelligence Labs. Charged with a mission to "bring personal superintelligence to everyone," in the words of Chief Executive \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2 , \uc2 MSL\uc2  is overseen by Chief AI Officer \uc2 Alexandr Wang\uc2 , who joined the company as part of a $14 billion deal for a stake in his former startup, \uc2 Scale AI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the forefront of the push to build a computer mind smarter than any human's is a team dubbed TBD Lab, which houses many of the researchers the company has lured from rival labs, in some cases with pay packages of tens or hundreds of millions of dollars.\par \par \uc2 TBD Lab, as in "to be determined," is spearheading work on the newest version of Llama, the company's large language model, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Wang sent a memo to employees recently that was viewed by The Wall Street Journal. Wang wrote that TBD Lab would be working alongside \uc2 Meta\uc2 's other AI teams on a variety of projects, including coming model releases, the extension of models' reasoning capabilities and development of AI agents.\par \par \uc2 "Already in the past month, I've seen meaningful progress in each of these collaborations," he wrote in the memo. "This enables us to be more technically ambitious, parallelize across several separate efforts and ultimately achieve frontier results more quickly."\par \par \uc2 The new Llama project is being led by Jack Rae, a hire to TBD Lab from \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 's \uc2 Google\uc2 . Members of \uc2 Meta\uc2 's existing Llama team and TBD Lab are working together on it, according to people familiar with the matter. The new model doesn't yet have an official name, but internally has been nicknamed Llama 4.5 by some and Llama 4.X by others.\par \par \uc2 Zuckerberg has described superintelligence as a revolutionary technology that "will improve all our existing systems and enable the creation and discovery of new things that aren't imaginable today."\par \par \uc2 To fuel its ambitions, \uc2 Meta\uc2  has been hiring aggressively from its rivals, offering researchers hundreds of millions of dollars and in at least two cases $1 billion pay packages over several years. The company has to date poached at least 18 researchers from \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  and a number from \uc2 Google\uc2 , including two recent additions, Tong He and Yuanzhong Xu, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Nine people from one of \uc2 Meta\uc2 's internal infrastructure teams were moved to the superintelligence unit after some of them got job offers from \uc2 Thinking Machines Lab\uc2 , a startup run by former \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  executive \uc2 Mira Murati\uc2 , according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Dave Arnold, a \uc2 Meta\uc2  spokesman, said the company had already been planning to move those people to TBD Lab and adjust their compensation regardless of recruitment offers they might have received.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250811el8b0000u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
89
