\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- Meta, Starbuck Settle Defamation Case --- Suit alleged chatbot incorrectly claimed he was involved in Jan. 6 Capitol riot\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joseph De Avila \par \uc2 443 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 August 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B9\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2  has settled a defamation lawsuit with conservative activist Robby Starbuck, who alleged the company's artificial intelligence chatbot falsely asserted he participated in the Jan. 6, 2021, riot at the U.S. Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Under the settlement, Starbuck will advise \uc2 Meta\uc2 , the owner of \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , on efforts to curb what they describe as political bias in its AI tools.\par \par \uc2 "Since engaging on these important issues with Robby, \uc2 Meta\uc2  has made tremendous strides to improve the accuracy of \uc2 Meta\uc2  AI and mitigate ideological and political bias," \uc2 Meta\uc2  and Starbuck said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Additional terms of the settlement weren't disclosed. Starbuck originally sought more than $5 million in damages for the lawsuit he filed in Delaware Superior Court in April.\par \par \uc2 During a CNBC interview Friday, Starbuck declined to say whether he had been paid by \uc2 Meta\uc2  as part of the settlement.\par \par \uc2 He said he had talked to \uc2 Meta\uc2  executives and engineers after the suit was filed about AI training and what needed to be done to address the issue.\par \par \uc2 The activist said his goal was ethical AI that remained neutral on political issues.\par \par \uc2 "We don't want a future where you've got AI putting the thumb on the scale when it comes to politics," he said.\par \par \uc2 Starbuck has gained attention for his efforts to pressure large companies to abandon their diversity, equity and inclusion policies.\par \par \uc2 He said he found out about the AI comments last summer when he was pushing for \uc2 Harley-Davidson\uc2  to change its DEI policies. A Harley dealer in Vermont posted a screenshot on X purportedly showing a Meta AI response saying that Starbuck was at the Capitol riot and that he was linked to QAnon.\par \par \uc2 Starbuck denied the allegations and said in a social-media post that "\uc2 Meta\uc2  will hear from my lawyers." He says Meta AI was still making the same unproven claims about him months later.\par \par \uc2 He took to social media to ask \uc2 Meta\uc2  executives, including Chief Executive \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2 , to take down the inaccurate information. Starbuck said his lawyer sent \uc2 Meta\uc2  a cease-and-desist letter.\par \par \uc2 Meta\uc2  has been working on removing political bias in its AI tools. AI systems have historically leaned left on contentious political and social topics based on how they have been trained, \uc2 Meta\uc2  said in a blog post in April.\par \par \uc2 "Our goal is to remove bias from our AI models and to make sure that Llama can understand and articulate both sides of a contentious issue," \uc2 Meta\uc2  said in the post, referring to its AI model.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250809el890002g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
