\par\par \uc2 Technology & Media\par \b \uc2 Peloton Posts Earnings Gain but Warns of Declining Sales\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rob Curran \par \uc2 326 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Peloton Interactive\uc2  swung to a fiscal fourth-quarter profit but warned that sales of its exercise machines and digital subscriptions are set to decline further in 2025, prompting it to lay off some employees and relocate operations in a bid to cut costs.\par \par \uc2 The fitness-equipment maker swung to a profit of $21.6 million, or 5 cents a share, from a loss of $31.9 million, or 8 cents a share, a year earlier. Analysts had, on average, anticipated a loss of 7 cents a share, according to a \uc2 FactSet\uc2  survey.\par \par \uc2 Revenue fell 5.7% to $606.9 million, topping the mean analyst estimate of $580 million, as per \uc2 FactSet\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Peloton plans to reduce the size of its work force in a cost-cutting push. Peloton also plans to cut indirect spending, and to relocate some operations.\par \par \uc2 "This is not a decision we came to lightly, as it impacts many talented team members, but we believe it is necessary for the long-term health of our business," Chief Executive \uc2 Peter Stern\uc2  said. The company estimated it would save $100 million annually from these cost cuts. Peloton will incur a restructuring charge initially.\par \par \uc2 For its fiscal first quarter ending in September, Peloton targeted revenue between $525 and $545 million.\par \par \uc2 The company expects paid connected fitness subscribers at the end of the September quarter in a range between 2.72 million and 2.73 million, down 6%.\par \par \uc2 For the fiscal year ending in 2026, Peloton targeted revenue in a range between $2.4 billion and $2.5 billion, 2% lower than the 2025 tally at the midpoint, as the company expects decreases in sales of its fitness machines and subscriptions to continue.\par \par \uc2 The maker of exercise machines also forecast fiscal 2026 gross margin of 51%, and adjusted earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization in a range between $400 million and $450 million.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250808el880001b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
