\par\par \b \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's AI Chief Poaches Google Talent\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sebastian Herrera and Katherine Blunt \par \uc2 852 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 August 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  hired one of the founders of \uc2 Google\uc2 's DeepMind to help it catch up in the AI race.\par \par \uc2 Now, \uc2 Mustafa Suleyman\uc2  is raiding his former shop for top talent.\par \par \uc2 Mirroring a tactic from \uc2 Meta\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2 , Suleyman has been personally calling recruits, pitching them on the idea that the fledgling AI division \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  created last year is a nimbler, more startup-like workplace than DeepMind has become under \uc2 Google\uc2 's ownership, people familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 Suleyman, head of \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  AI, has offered heftier pay and the opportunity to help turn \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's Copilot chatbot into a more formidable competitor to \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's ChatGPT, the people said.\par \par \uc2 The company has poached at least two dozen executives and other employees from \uc2 Google\uc2  in the past several months, with most having worked at DeepMind, the people said. Among them are Adam Sadovsky, a former \uc2 Google DeepMind\uc2  distinguished engineer, and Amar Subramanya, formerly vice president of engineering at \uc2 Google\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Suleyman's recruitment offensive is the latest salvo in the increasingly frenzied battle for AI talent. Multitrillion-dollar Silicon Valley giants are jousting with startups such as \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  and \uc2 Anthropic\uc2  over the limited pool of engineers who understand the inner workings of so-called deep learning models. Individual pay packages have run into nine figures, and companies are spending tens of billions more on data centers in the quest to be the first to build a machine that exhibits humanlike intelligence.\par \par \uc2 Suleyman, who spent about nine years at DeepMind, has considerable leeway to make big-dollar offers to recruit talent. CEO \uc2 Satya Nadella\uc2  has given him autonomy to build an AI operation that can compete with top players like \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , which \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  also counts as a close partner. Suleyman's team is based primarily in Mountain View, Calif., some 800 miles from \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's corporate seat in Redmond, Wash., and has operations in London.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  spokesman said that all of its senior leaders "have equal ability to recruit talent and manage their teams in a way that works successfully for their business and their people alike."\par \par \uc2 The pay packages \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  has offered its newest recruits haven't been on the scale of those offered by \uc2 Meta\uc2 , which has promised some researchers $300-million contracts, people who have received the offers said. But they have been far above the going rate at DeepMind, especially for longer-tenured employees, those people said.\par \par \uc2 According to Levels.fyi, which tracks tech industry compensation, average salary companywide is higher at \uc2 Google\uc2  than at \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The recruits will primarily work on consumer-facing products such as the Copilot chatbot, \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's answer to ChatGPT and Gemini. Suleyman is in charge of the consumer version of Copilot; the company also has enterprise versions for its 365 products and \uc2 GitHub\uc2  developer platform. Last week, the company said Copilot would be further integrated into search functions on its Edge browser, allowing the AI tool to browse through open tabs to help compare hotel options, for example.\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  AI, Suleyman has promised recruiting targets more freedom to do their work within nimbler teams, a startup vibe several described as appealing.\par \par \uc2 "The culture here is refreshingly low ego yet bursting with ambition," Subramanya wrote in a \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2  post in late July announcing his role at \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DeepMind's workforce has swelled to around 6,000 employees as what had been a relatively small lab became the core of \uc2 Google\uc2 's AI push. Two of the candidates \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  successfully recruited said they were eager to work in a less bureaucratic environment.\par \par \uc2 Twenty years ago, it was \uc2 Google\uc2  that was luring \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  workers with the promise of more action and less bureaucracy, said \uc2 Laszlo Bock\uc2 , former senior vice president of people operations at \uc2 Google\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  has come to resemble the more staid \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  of years past, pairing enormous profits with an organization that can be slow-moving, hierarchical and political, Bock said. "It feels much more like a company run by a finance person than an engineer," he said.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  said its attrition rates are below industry average and that it has hired a number of employees from \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We are excited that we are able to attract the world's leading AI talent, including researchers and engineers who come from rival labs," a spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 Earnings reports in recent weeks showed how the AI boom is transforming \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2  parent \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 . Both companies reported surging revenue driven in part by demand for cloud computing services tied to AI. They also previewed plans to increase their outlays on data centers, with \uc2 Alphabet\uc2  raising its capital-expenditure expectations for the year to $85 billion from $75 billion and \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  forecasting more than $30 billion in spending during the current quarter.\par \par \uc2 Lacking the profit to fuel its own capital and talent needs, \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  has been forced to turn to investors once again. The venture firm Thrive Capital is in talks to buy shares in \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  at a $500 billion valuation, people familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg News earlier reported the sale.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250807el870001t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
